// The Simulate panel's slow-seek line (camui::slowSeekText, the panel's simSlowSeek; sim_tool.h slowSeekText) from a
// real run, not an injected report (RunRequest::seekReport): a finishing-heavy program, modelled on the finishing
// stress program of tests/unit/sim/simulator_bench_test.cpp (finishProgram), run through the real session
// (api::cam_sim::SimSession, as the panel runs it) on a real document at the High preset's cell, then at Medium's.
//
//   The document: a 300 x 200 x 30 plate with a 260 x 160 pocket 15 deep (its floor at Z 15). Operations, each
//   generated by the CAM engine: a pocket2d roughing of the pocket in twelve 0.5 mm levels with a 16 mm end mill,
//   leaving 9 mm on the floor (down to Z 24, as finishProgram's pocket), then three ball-end rasters over 220 x 120 mm
//   of a wavy surface 2 to 6 mm under that (a 10 mm ball along X at 1 mm steps, +0.4 mm; a 6 mm ball along Y at
//   0.4 mm, +0.15; along X at 0.3 mm, on it), made by a test-only operation type ("test.raster": the bench's raster,
//   approached from 2 mm above the roughed floor). About 180k moves, every motion through the safety checks and the
//   gouge test as in the app (the surface stays above the part's floor: no gouge).
//   High (0.05 mm): every raster line changes a band of tiles nothing else shares, so the keyframes pass High's 2 GB
//   budget and are thinned (simulator.h KEYFRAMES: twice on the reference machine, worst seek about 0.3 s): the line
//   is there, and its time is the run's own estimate (SeekReport::worstSeekMs), plausible (0.1 s to a minute) and
//   rounded as slowSeekText says. Medium (0.1 mm): within its budget, not thinned: no line.
//
// What it costs (Release, 32 hardware threads, 8 workers, measured when written; the test prints its own line): about
// 50 s in all (the High run 33 s, thinned once, estimate 0.9 s; Medium 11 s, not thinned, 84 ms), the process peaking
// at 2.5 GB: thinning at High means the keyframes passed its 2 GB budget, so no program that shows the line at High
// can need much less. It is in the slow tier (tests/tiers.cmake). Whether the High line appears depends on the seek
// estimate passing High's 100 ms, which is a wall-clock measurement (three times over on the reference machine, and
// only larger on a slower or busier one): so it is labelled bench as well, which CI leaves out. Nothing here checks a
// time limit.
#include "cam/sim_logic.h"
#include "engine_test_util.h"
#include "parametric_test_util.h"

